The side effects of all earlier expressions must be made visible to later expressions past
sequence points (in a single threaded context)

List of sequence points is described here though I do not know if that is a complete list:
http://publications.gbdirect.co.uk/c_book/chapter8/sequence_points.html

It is however not true that the compiler *must* writeback register to memory, the rule
says side effects must be visible so as-if rule optimizations apply!

